{"judgments": [
 {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The Preamble equates \"Fund\" with \"Plan\" as a single defined term, whereas Sections 1.20 and 1.22 define \"Plan\" as the rules of benefits and \"Fund\"/\"Trust Fund\" as the pool of assets. A court asked which meaning governs a reference to the \"Fund\" would have to reconcile the Preamble with those definitions.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.23}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The recital says the Collective Bargaining Agreements \"establish the Plan,\" but Section 1.20 and Section 7.2(2) give the Board alone the design and adoption of the Plan. A party could argue the recital controls and makes the bargained agreements the source of Plan terms.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.26}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The recital contemplates that \"the Union and the Association will execute a Trust Agreement and appoint Trustees,\" while Section 3.3 and the Preamble treat the named individuals as parties and Section 3.1 splits selection between Association and Union. A court could be asked whether the Association's and Union's appointment power derives from the recital or the operative sections.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The recital limits the Trust to the \"exclusive purpose of providing pension and retirement benefits,\" while Section 4.1(a) and Section 2.2 permit \"such other related benefits as the Board may from time to time determine.\" A party could argue the recital's narrower statement of purpose controls the operative benefit power.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c006", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The recital rests the amendment power on \"Paragraph 18 of the Trust Agreement,\" a provision that has no counterpart in the restated instrument, whose amendment power is Section 10.1 and requires a unanimous Board vote plus three provisos. A court would have to decide whether the recited authority or Section 10.1 governs the validity of this restatement and later amendments.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c007", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Defining \"Administrator\" to include the Board itself cannot be squared with Article 7, which allocates distinct responsibilities to \"The Administrator\" (7.1) and \"The Board\" (7.2), or with Section 5.3(c), which has the Board engage a person as Administrator. Whether a duty assigned to the Administrator is a duty of the Board turns on which reading prevails.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c008", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c009", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The definition names the \"Publishers' Association of New York,\" omitting \"City,\" while the Preamble and Section 12.8(d) name the \"Publishers' Association of New York City.\" The mismatch leaves the identity of the defined \"Association\" open on the face of the instrument.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.19}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c010", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Both the Chairman and Secretary of the Board\" is ambiguous as to whether the two officers constitute a single Authorized Person who must act jointly or are each separately authorized. The same sentence then adds \"any individual Trustee ... duly authorized by the Board,\" which points the other way.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c011", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Such other person or entity who, as a result of his relationship to the Covered Employee, is entitled under the terms of the Plan\" states no boundary on what relationship qualifies and is circular, deferring entirely to the unstated Plan. The word \"entity\" also sits oddly against a definition keyed to a personal relationship.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.15}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c012", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c013", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The definition refers to the \"Internal Revenue Code of 1936,\" a statute that does not exist; the sections cited throughout (401(a), 501(a), 404, 4975, 407) are provisions of the 1986 Code. The mechanical error leaves the governing statute unidentified on the face of the definition.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c014", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The definition counts an agreement as a \"Collective Bargaining Agreement\" only if it \"is acceptable to the Board,\" which cannot be squared with Section 9.1, under which the contribution rate is \"at all times\" governed by the Collective Bargaining Agreements and their amendments and modifications regardless of Board approval. Whether a side memorandum modifying contribution rates binds the Fund depends on which provision controls.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.33}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c015", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The definition incorporates the Collective Trust's own agreement by reference \"to the extent that the provisions thereof are not inconsistent with the terms of this Agreement,\" without saying who decides inconsistency or which term yields. A court would have to construe that proviso against the Collective Trust trustees' \"sole and exclusive authority\" granted in the same definition.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c016", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This definition requires a Committee to contain only \"at least one Employer Trustee and one Union Trustee,\" while Section 5.6(b) requires \"an equal number\" of each. A Committee of one Employer and two Union Trustees satisfies Article 1 but violates Section 5.6(b).", "type": 2, "prob": 0.21}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c017", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Covered under the terms of a Collective Bargaining Agreement ... requiring contributions on behalf of said individual\" is circular and does not say whether coverage turns on the employee's job category designated under Section 2.4(c) or on contributions actually being owed. Employees in a unit for whom no contribution is in fact made fall in an undefined space.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.17}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c018", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The definition allows a broker-dealer to be selected as a \"Corporate Trustee (as that term is defined in Section 3.12),\" but Section 3.12(a) permits only \"a bank or trust company located within the United States\" to be appointed Corporate Trustee. The two provisions cannot both be given effect as to broker-dealers.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.26}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c019", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Employer\" is defined to mean any employer required to contribute under a Collective Bargaining Agreement, while Section 2.4 makes participation depend on the employer being \"acceptable to the Trustees\" and executing a Board-approved agreement. Whether an employer obligated by a bargaining agreement the Board never approved is an \"Employer\" cannot be answered from one provision alone.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c020", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The definition ties Employer Trustees to designation \"pursuant to Section 3.3(a),\" which names only two individuals, whereas successors are designated under Section 3.9 by certificate filed with the Board. The cross-reference leaves later Employer Trustees outside the literal definition.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c021", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c022", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Foreign Securities\" is defined by reference to ERISA Section 404(b) and 29 C.F.R. 2550.404b-1, which regulate where indicia of ownership of plan assets may be maintained rather than defining any category of security. The definition therefore supplies no usable boundary for the term used in Sections 1.21(h) and 5.5(p).", "type": 1, "prob": 0.17}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c023", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Instructions\" are defined as \"written communications signed by an Authorized Person\" yet expressly include telex and like transmissions that bear no signature, requiring only that the receiver can verify the sender \"with a reasonable degree of certainty.\" Whether an unsigned electronic message is a valid Instruction is left ambiguous.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c024", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The definition makes a written acknowledgment of fiduciary status a condition of being an \"Investment Manager,\" while Section 8.3 says only that the Board \"may require\" such a certificate. Whether a manager who never delivered the acknowledgment is an Investment Manager (and whether the Board's liability disclaimers in Sections 8.5 and 8.8 then apply) turns on that conflict.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c025", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The account is described as segregated \"by the Trustees,\" while Section 8.1(b) directs the Board to segregate or to request the Custodian to segregate the assets. Whether assets a Custodian has segregated constitute an Investment Manager Account is left open.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c026", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Plan\" is defined as rules \"from time to time adopted by the Board,\" which cannot be squared with the second recital's statement that the Collective Bargaining Agreements \"establish the Plan.\" A dispute over whether bargained terms are Plan terms would require reconciling the two.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.18}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c027", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The eleven enumerated categories are prefaced by \"including, but not limited to\" and closed by catch-all subsection (k), so it is unclear whether an instrument unlike any listed item is a \"Security.\" The ejusdem generis tension is sharpened by the express ERISA limits attached only to employer stock and employer obligations.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.15}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c028", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Trust Fund\" is limited to cash and property that \"shall have been deposited\" or is held by a Custodian, which says nothing about contributions due but unpaid that Article 9 elsewhere treats as owing \"to the Trust Fund.\" Whether delinquent contributions are Fund assets cannot be answered from this definition.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.21}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c029", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The definition covers successors \"and assigns\" of a personal fiduciary office and conditions their status on appointment \"as provided in Section 3.9 or Section 3.10,\" leaving unclear whether an individual can assign a trusteeship at all. The parenthetical condition also makes the definition read as though there are no Trustees until successors are appointed.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.14}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c030", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Union\" is defined to include \"any affiliates thereof\" without any test of affiliation, so which labor organizations can select Union Trustees or execute a Collective Bargaining Agreement under Section 1.8 is left open. The term matters wherever the Agreement gives the Union rights, as in Section 9.8 and Section 10.3(a)(2).", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c031", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The definition ties Union Trustees to designation \"pursuant to Section 3.3(b),\" yet Section 3.8 provides that the Union Trustees \"shall be\" the incumbent officers of the Union and Section 3.10 governs successors. The three provisions give three different sources of Union Trustee status.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.20}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c032", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c033", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Certain pension and related benefits\" leaves \"related benefits\" undefined and unbounded, and \"certain\" gives no criterion for which pension benefits the exclusive purpose covers. Section 4.1(a) compounds the problem by leaving \"related benefits\" to the Board's determination.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.21}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c034", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause provides that anything inconsistent with Code Sections 401(a) and 501(a) means \"this Agreement shall be deemed amended,\" which cannot be squared with Section 10.1, under which amendment requires a unanimous vote of the Board subject to three provisos. A court would have to decide whether an automatic deemed amendment can occur without the Section 10.1 process.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c035", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The ERISA \"deemed amended\" sentence conflicts with Section 10.1, which makes amendment of this Agreement depend on a unanimous vote of the Board, and it supplies no mechanism for determining what the deemed amendment says. Whether such a self-executing amendment is effective would have to be construed against Section 10.1.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.26}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c036", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Operating as a \"jointly-administered\" fund within Section 302(c) of the LMRA presupposes equal representation, but Section 3.1 composes the Board of two Employer Trustees and three Union Trustees. The two provisions cannot both be given literal effect.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.31}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c037", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Participation is conditioned on the Employer being \"acceptable to the Trustees\" and executing a Board-approved agreement, while Section 1.13 makes any employer required to contribute under a bargaining agreement an \"Employer\" without Board acceptance. Whether an unapproved employer participates in the Trust turns on which provision governs.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c038", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"An Employer shall be deemed to have\" reviewed, adopted and agreed states no triggering act — no signature, contribution or other event is identified as producing the deemed agreement. Whether the deeming follows from Section 2.4 participation, from making a contribution, or from something else is unstated.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c039", "issues": [
   {"issue": "A Board of two Employer Trustees and three Union Trustees cannot be squared with Section 2.3's undertaking that the Trust be operated as a \"jointly-administered\" fund under LMRA Section 302(c), nor with Section 10.1(c)'s bar on amendments producing \"unequal voting power\" between the two groups. Amendment No. 4 later recomposed the Board as two and two, confirming the tension.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.33}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c040", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c041", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The named Association designees are superseded by Amendment No. 4's replacement of Section 3.3, which designates different individuals, so the section as printed no longer describes the Board. Which text governs at a given date must be worked out across the two instruments.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.14}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c042", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This subsection names three Union Trustees, while Amendment No. 4 replaces Section 3.3 with two Union designees and Amendment No. 4's Section 3.1 caps Union Trustees at two. The provisions cannot both be given effect.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c043", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Written appointments need only be provided to the Board \"as soon as practicable after the appointments,\" a standard with no measurable boundary, while Section 3.11 vests a successor with full powers only upon designation and written acceptance filed with the Board. When a successor's authority begins is left uncertain.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c044", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Service continues until \"death, incapacity, resignation or removal,\" but \"incapacity\" is undefined and no person or procedure is identified to determine it. Section 3.9 and 3.10 likewise speak of a Trustee who has \"become incapable of acting\" without a mechanism.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.18}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c045", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The final sentence deems a Trustee to have resigned when \"the Contributing Employer which designated him\" ceases to contribute, but under Sections 3.1 and 3.3(a) Employer Trustees are designated by the Association, not by any individual Contributing Employer. The deemed-resignation trigger cannot be applied to the Trustees this Agreement actually creates.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.32}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c046", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c047", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Although captioned \"Removal,\" this section dictates that the Union Trustees \"shall be\" the incumbent president, vice president and secretary-treasurer, which cannot be squared with Section 3.1's grant of free selection to the Union or with Section 3.3(b)'s designation of named individuals. Section 3.10's successor mechanism, in which the principal officer designates, conflicts further.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.29}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c048", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c049", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The section says the principal officer \"shall designate a successor Union Trustee\" and in the same sentence that \"a Successor Union Trustee shall be elected from the full-time officers of the Union.\" Designation and election are inconsistent methods, and the provision does not say which prevails.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c050", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c051", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Only \"a bank or trust company located within the United States\" may be appointed Corporate Trustee, while Section 1.12 defines \"Custodian\" to include broker-dealers \"selected by the Board as a Corporate Trustee.\" The eligibility of a broker-dealer to serve in that role cannot be settled from either provision alone.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c052", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The power to let a Corporate Trustee hold the Fund \"as sole trustee of a trust separate from the Fund created by this Trust Agreement\" cannot be squared with Section 5.1, which vests the Board with all right, title and interest in the contributions and requires it to hold them in trust hereunder, or with Section 1.22's definition of the Trust Fund. Whether assets so transferred remain subject to this Agreement is left in doubt.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c053", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The declaration that the Trustees are \"forever released and discharged from any responsibility or liability\" for transferred assets cannot be squared with Section 5.7's prudent-person standard of care or with Section 7.2(4) and (13), which make the Board responsible for designating and monitoring fiduciaries. A court would have to decide whether the release survives those duties.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.23}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c054", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c055", "issues": [
