 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c123", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This section makes the contribution rate governed \"at all times\" by the Collective Bargaining Agreements and their \"amendments, supplements, and modifications,\" while Section 1.8 recognizes as a Collective Bargaining Agreement only one that \"is acceptable to the Board.\" Whether a side memorandum reapportioning or altering the rate binds the Fund without Board acceptance cannot be answered from either provision alone.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.40},
   {"issue": "\"Amendments, supplements, and modifications\" is left undefined, so it is unclear whether letter agreements, memoranda of agreement and reapportionment understandings between an Employer and the Union count as such. The final sentence's promise that nothing here changes \"any of the terms or provisions of any such agreement\" sharpens the question of what documents are in the set.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c124", "issues": [
